AB  - Applied Machine Learning (AML) has become an integral part of modern society, revolutionizing various aspects of our daily lives. In the real world, AML is utilized across numerous industries, including healthcare, finance, transportation, and entertainment. For instance, in healthcare, machine learning algorithms analyze patient data to predict disease outbreaks, optimize treatment plans, and enhance diagnostic accuracy. In finance, AML is used for fraud detection, credit scoring, and algorithmic trading, enabling quicker decision-making and improved risk management. The transportation sector leverages machine learning for traffic prediction, route optimization, and autonomous vehicles, ultimately enhancing efficiency and safety. These applications demonstrate how AML enhances productivity and decisionmaking, shaping a more efficient and interconnected world.
